1
00:00:00,773 --> 00:00:02,903
♪ It's the eye of the tiger ♪

2
00:00:02,909 --> 00:00:05,039
♪ It's the ear of the bat ♪

3
00:00:05,045 --> 00:00:07,375
♪ It's the whiskers
of the catfish ♪

4
00:00:07,381 --> 00:00:10,251
♪ And the walrus... ♪

5
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:14,490
(Howard:)Hang on. Not that your song
isn't terrible-- it is...

6
00:00:15,755 --> 00:00:19,525
(Howard:)...but how do you mention bats
and leave out sonar?

7
00:00:19,526 --> 00:00:21,526
(Sheldon:)You didn't let me finish.

8
00:00:21,528 --> 00:00:25,568
♪ And also regarding the bat ♪

9
00:00:25,565 --> 00:00:27,695
♪ It has sonar. ♪

10
00:00:29,402 --> 00:00:30,832
KOOTHRAPPALI:
Hey.

11
00:00:30,837 --> 00:00:31,967
(Sheldon:)Hello.

12
00:00:31,972 --> 00:00:34,202
(Raj:)Look,

13
00:00:34,207 --> 00:00:37,107
(Raj:)I know you guys are upset,
but we've talked about it,

14
00:00:37,110 --> 00:00:38,710
(Raj:)and we think it'd be beneficial

15
00:00:38,712 --> 00:00:40,842
(Raj:)for you to be part
of the project.

16
00:00:41,881 --> 00:00:45,421
(Howard:)Well, well, well,
did you hear that, Sheldon?

17
00:00:45,419 --> 00:00:47,919
(Sheldon:)I'm sorry. I was trying
to think of what rhymes

18
00:00:47,921 --> 00:00:50,521
with "nose of the aardvark."

19
00:00:50,524 --> 00:00:51,824
LEONARD:
We want you

20
00:00:51,825 --> 00:00:54,025
(Leonard:)back on the project with us.

21
00:00:54,027 --> 00:00:59,027
(Howard:)Well, well, well, did
you hear that, Howard?

